{% comment %}
  ==================================================================
  GS REVIEWS
  Consolidates THREE v3 snippets into one (audit ref DUP-011):
    snippets/reviews.liquid               (2.8 KB)
    snippets/reviews-count.liquid         (3.0 KB)
    snippets/reviews-without-count.liquid (2.9 KB)

  All three contained the same star-rendering loop, differing only in
  which variable they read and what text they appended.

  USAGE:
    render 'gs-reviews', cardProduct: product                  stars only
    render 'gs-reviews', cardProduct: product, showCount: true stars + "12 reviews"
    render 'gs-reviews', cardProduct: product, showRating: true stars + "4.8/5"
    Optional: extraClass: 'd-block d-md-none'

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  REVISION 2026-08-13 - CARRIES ITS OWN STYLESHEET
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  The star styles lived only in gs-card-product.css, which loads when a
  product CARD renders. The PDP renders this snippet directly, so on a
  product page the stars had no styling and fell back to a VERTICAL
  BULLETED LIST. A snippet renderable from anywhere must carry its own
  CSS. Shopify de-duplicates repeated stylesheet_tag output.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  BUG FIXED FROM v3: RATINGS ROUNDED DOWN A FULL STAR
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  All three v3 snippets used:
      if decimal >= 0.3 and decimal <= 0.7 -> half star
  Anything above 0.7 fell through to NOTHING, so a 4.8-rated product
  rendered four filled stars and one empty - it displayed as 4 stars.

  Corrected thresholds:
      decimal <  0.25        no extra star
      0.25 - 0.75            half star
      decimal >= 0.75        full star

  ACTION: this changes displayed ratings across the store. Products at
  x.75-x.99 gain a visible star. Correct, but tell merchandising.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  BUG FIXED FROM v3: GLOBAL CSS LEAKING FROM INSIDE SVG
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  The half-star SVG carried an inline <defs><style> defining `.d` and
  `.e`. A <style> inside inline SVG is NOT scoped - it applies to the
  whole document. The definitions also CONFLICTED: reviews-count.liquid
  declared `.d { fill: none }`, the other two `.d { fill: #ddd }`, so
  half-star appearance depended on which snippet rendered last.
  All <style> blocks removed; fills are plain path attributes.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  OTHER FIXES
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  - VARIABLE MISMATCH: two snippets read `product`, one read
    `cardProduct`. Rendering the wrong one from a card context silently
    produced nothing. Unified on `cardProduct`.
  - PDP state leaked into a card snippet: reviews-without-count.liquid
    referenced block.settings.sticky_form and section.settings.sticky_type.
    Removed; use `extraClass` instead.
  - Added role="img" + aria-label so the rating is announced as a value
    rather than read out as five empty list items.
  - A filter cannot appear inside an if/elsif condition, so the
    half-star index is precomputed into `half_index`.
==================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  unless cardProduct
    break
  endunless

  assign rating_count = cardProduct.metafields.reviews.rating_count | plus: 0
  assign rating_value = cardProduct.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating
-%}

{%- if rating_count > 0 and rating_value -%}
  {{ 'gs-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {%- liquid
    assign full_stars = rating_value | floor
    assign decimal = rating_value | modulo: 1
    assign half_star = false

    if decimal >= 0.75
      assign full_stars = full_stars | plus: 1
    elsif decimal >= 0.25
      assign half_star = true
    endif

    assign half_index = full_stars | plus: 1

    assign review_word = 'products.product.reviews' | t
    if rating_count == 1
      assign review_word = 'products.product.review' | t
    endif
  -%}

  <div
    class="product-reviews-badge rating-wrapper{% if extraClass %} {{ extraClass }}{% endif %}"
    role="img"
    aria-label="{{ rating_value }} {{ 'products.product.out_of_5_stars' | t }}, {{ rating_count }} {{ review_word }}"
  >
    <ul class="unstylish-list star-rating" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
        <li>
          {%- if i <= full_stars -%}
            <svg class="fill-review" viewBox="0 0 380 362" width="15" height="19" focusable="false">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" fill="currentColor" d="m204.7 10.5l37.5 116.1l122-0.3c15.4 0 21.2 19.1 7.7 28.9l-97.5 70.5l37.9 115.9c4.9 14.8-12.9 26.5-24.6 16.5l-97.6-71.2l-98.6 71.9c-13.4 9.7-28.2-3.4-22.6-20.4l36.9-112.7l-98.8-71.5c-12.6-9.1-5.2-28.9 10.1-27.9l120.9 0.3l37.5-116.1c4.5-14.2 24.7-14.1 29.2 0z"/>
            </svg>
          {%- elsif half_star and i == half_index -%}
            <svg class="half-fill-review" viewBox="0 0 19.89 19.01" width="15" height="19" focusable="false">
              <path fill="currentColor" d="M9.18,.56l-1.97,6.09-6.35-.02c-.8-.05-1.19,.99-.53,1.46l5.19,3.75-1.94,5.92c-.29,.89,.48,1.58,1.19,1.07l5.17-3.77V0c-.32,0-.65,.19-.76,.56Z"/>
              <path fill="#dddddd" d="M19.08,6.63l-6.4,.02L10.71,.56C10.59,.19,10.27,0,9.94,0V15.07h0l5.12,3.73c.61,.52,1.55-.09,1.29-.87l-1.99-6.08,5.12-3.7c.71-.51,.4-1.52-.4-1.52Z"/>
            </svg>
          {%- else -%}
            <svg class="unfill-review" viewBox="0 0 380 362" width="15" height="19" focusable="false">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" fill="#dddddd" d="m204.7 10.5l37.5 116.1l122-0.3c15.4 0 21.2 19.1 7.7 28.9l-97.5 70.5l37.9 115.9c4.9 14.8-12.9 26.5-24.6 16.5l-97.6-71.2l-98.6 71.9c-13.4 9.7-28.2-3.4-22.6-20.4l36.9-112.7l-98.8-71.5c-12.6-9.1-5.2-28.9 10.1-27.9l120.9 0.3l37.5-116.1c4.5-14.2 24.7-14.1 29.2 0z"/>
            </svg>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {%- if showRating -%}
      <span class="reviewbox text-xsmall">{{ rating_value }}/5</span>
    {%- elsif showCount -%}
      <span class="reviewbox text-xsmall">{{ rating_count }} {{ review_word }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
